"Internal Error ()\nciteturn31443view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://openai.com/news/rss.xml\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://openai.com/news/rss.xml: (400) Unsupported content-type: text/xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nResearch \\ Anthropic (https://www.anthropic.com/research)\nciteturn31443view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.anthropic.com/research\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 56\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content cite1†Skip to footer L1: \nL2:   * Research\nL3:   * cite2†Policy L4:   * Commitments\nL5:   * Learn\nL6:   * cite3†News L7: \nL8: cite4†Try Claude†claude.ai L9: \nL10: # Research\nL11: \nL12: Our research teams investigate the safety, inner workings, and societal impacts of AI models—so that artificial intelligence has a positive impact as it becomes increasingly capable.\nL13: \nL14: Research teams:cite5†Alignment cite6†Economics cite7†Interpretability cite8†Societal Impacts cite9†Frontier Red Team L15: ### Alignment\nL16: \nL17: The Alignment team works to understand the risks of AI models and develop ways to ensure that future ones remain helpful, honest, and harmless.\nL18: \nL19: ### Economics\nL20: \nL21: The Economics team studies how AI is reshaping the economy, including work, productivity, and economic opportunity.\nL22: \nL23: ### Frontier Red Team\nL24: \nL25: The Frontier Red Team analyzes the implications of frontier AI models for cybersecurity, biosecurity, and autonomous systems.\nL26: ### Interpretability\nL27: \nL28: The mission of the Interpretability team is to understand how large language models work internally, as a foundation for AI safety and positive outcomes.\nL29: ### Societal Impacts\nL30: \nL31: Working closely with the Anthropic Policy and Safeguards teams, Societal Impacts is a technical research team that explores how AI is used in the real world.\nL32: \nL33: cite10†Image: Scenarios for our Economic Future L34: cite11†Scenarios for our Economic Future Anthropic’s Economics team is sharing a new model of how AI may affect economic growth, jobs, wages, and more by 2030. The model lets you explore the scenarios, tell us what you think will happen, and see how your answers compare to +10,000 Americans. L35: cite12†Societal ImpactsSep 29, 2026 What do you want from AI? We’re launching a new study using Anthropic Interviewer to learn from your experiences with AI. cite13†EconomicsSep 24, 2026 Project Swap: What happens when agents trade for us?To see what works and what breaks when agents are sent into a market, we made a miniature market of Claudes. cite14†ScienceSep 23, 2026 Claude discovers a novel enzyme system with CRISPR-like repeats We’re announcing a new life sciences research group and laboratory at Anthropic.\nL36: This post introduces the team behind this work and shares early results in which Claude discovered a novel enzyme system with properties reminiscent of CRISPR. cite15†Sep 17, 2026 Measurements for understanding the pace of AI development inside frontier labs Today, the world can’t see what’s going on inside AI labs. Anthropic is proposing new metrics that would give the public visibility into frontier AI development. L37: ## Publications\nL38: \nL39: Search[Input: Search]\nL40: \nL41: Date Category Title\nL42:   * cite16†Oct 1, 2026Science Claude-shaped science L43:   * cite17†Sep 30, 2026Economics What work can robots do? L44:   * cite12†Sep 29, 2026Societal Impacts What do you want from AI? L45:   * cite18†Sep 29, 2026Frontier Red Team GLM-5.3 and the spread of advanced cyber capabilities L46:   * cite19†Sep 25, 2026Science Yes, Claude can do Nine Loops L47:   * cite13†Sep 24, 2026Economics Project Swap: What happens when agents trade for us? L48:   * cite20†Sep 17, 2026Science How Claude is uplifting biomolecular modelin